    "earlier": [
     {
      "by": "claude",
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "note": "Hits read: process enumeration and memory info are psutil's purpose; the native module's socket import lists connections (net_connections). Content review only."
     }
    ],
    "note": "macOS arm64 and Windows amd64 wheels of the reviewed version: the same 16 members, with _psutil_osx resp. _psutil_windows in place of _psutil_linux (the platform backend). Python identical (Windows CRLF only); the 11 'new' keys are the reviewed process-enumeration hits, CRLF-changed. The Mach-O's socket import lists connections (net_connections), as on Linux; the .pyd's AdjustTokenPrivileges/OpenProcessToken (capa: acquire debug privileges) is psutil's documented SeDebugPrivilege for reading other processes, TerminateProcess is Process.kill(), IPHLPAPI/WS2_32 list connections. No .pth, no hook. No attestation: content review only."
   },
